IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb2-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part VII, section 49 -- SECURITY CERTIFICATES
-- (the right to one, how it is signed, what it must state, what restrictions bind a transferee, fractional
-- shares and scrip). Layer 1.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RULE. Named `<what it works out> within s <section>`. A requirement ("shall be stated")
-- is encoded as a rule that is TRUE when it is met, and is TRUE when the requirement does not apply to
-- the case. A bar ("is not entitled", "is not effective") is encoded as TRUE when the bar applies.
-- Where a provision says what follows in a stated case, the rule is TRUE when that case holds and the
-- provision applies; FALSE means only that this provision does not apply, never that the opposite holds.
-- A rule whose result is a MAYBE returns NOTHING where the text is silent for the case.
-- Within one module, a rule that depends on another section's rule calls it and takes its inputs; a plain
-- input stands in for another section only across modules, and says so ("out of range" or "to avoid a cycle").

§ `s 49 Security certificates`

§§ `s 49(1) Rights of holder`

-- Every security holder may choose, for the securities of the corporation they hold, between a
-- certificate that complies with the Act and a non-transferable written acknowledgment of their right to
-- obtain one. NOTHING: the person is not a security holder of the corporation, so s 49(1) gives nothing.
-- src:738 | Rights of holder
-- src:739 | 49 (1) Every security holder is entitled at their option to a security certificate that complies with this Act or a non-transferable written acknowledgment of their right to obtain such a security certificate from a corporation in respect of the securities of that corporation held by them.
@ref CBCA s 49(1) (src:738-739)
DECLARE `What a security holder may be given under s 49(1)` IS ONE OF
    `a security certificate that complies with the Act`
    `a non-transferable written acknowledgment of the right to obtain a security certificate`

-- src:738 | Rights of holder
-- src:739 | 49 (1) Every security holder is entitled at their option to a security certificate that complies with this Act or a non-transferable written acknowledgment of their right to obtain such a security certificate from a corporation in respect of the securities of that corporation held by them.
@ref CBCA s 49(1) (src:738-739)
GIVEN `the person is a security holder of the corporation in respect of securities of the corporation held by them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder opts for a security certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `What a security holder may be given under s 49(1)`
`what the corporation must give the security holder at their option within s 49(1)` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is a security holder of the corporation in respect of securities of the corporation held by them`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the holder opts for a security certificate`
         THEN JUST `a security certificate that complies with the Act`
         ELSE JUST `a non-transferable written acknowledgment of the right to obtain a security certificate`

§§ `s 49(2) Maximum fee for certificate by regulation`

-- The corporation may charge a fee for a certificate issued in respect of a transfer, not exceeding the
-- prescribed amount. The prescribed amount is in the regulations, which are not among the sources: it is
-- a plain input. NOTHING: the certificate is not issued in respect of a transfer, so s 49(2) is silent.
-- src:740 | Maximum fee for certificate by regulation
-- src:741 | (2) A corporation may charge a fee, not exceeding the prescribed amount, for a security certificate issued in respect of a transfer.
@ref CBCA s 49(2) (src:740-741)
GIVEN `the certificate is issued in respect of a transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fee the corporation charges in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the prescribed maximum fee in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the corporation may charge the fee within s 49(2)` MEANS
    IF `the certificate is issued in respect of a transfer`
    THEN JUST (`the fee the corporation charges in dollars` AT MOST `the prescribed maximum fee in dollars`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 49(3) Joint holders`

-- src:742 | Joint holders
-- src:743 | (3) A corporation is not required to issue more than one security certificate in respect of securities held jointly by several persons, and delivery of a certificate to one of several joint holders is sufficient delivery to all.
@ref CBCA s 49(3) (src:742-743)
GIVEN `the securities are held jointly by several persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation need not issue more than one security certificate within s 49(3)` MEANS
    `the securities are held jointly by several persons`

-- src:742 | Joint holders
-- src:743 | (3) A corporation is not required to issue more than one security certificate in respect of securities held jointly by several persons, and delivery of a certificate to one of several joint holders is sufficient delivery to all.
@ref CBCA s 49(3) (src:742-743)
GIVEN `the securities are held jointly by several persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate is delivered to at least one of the joint holders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`delivery to one joint holder is sufficient delivery to all within s 49(3)` MEANS
        `the securities are held jointly by several persons`
    AND `the certificate is delivered to at least one of the joint holders`

§§ `s 49(4) Signatures`

-- At least one of (a) a director or officer, (b) a registrar, transfer agent or branch transfer agent (or an
-- individual on their behalf) or (c) a trustee who certifies it under a trust indenture, must have signed;
-- or the signature may be printed or otherwise mechanically reproduced on the certificate. Each input is
-- "that person's signature is on the certificate", signed by hand or printed or mechanically reproduced.
-- src:744 | Signatures
-- src:745 | (4) A security certificate shall be signed by at least one of the following persons, or the signature shall be printed or otherwise mechanically reproduced on the certificate:
-- src:746 | (a) a director or officer of the corporation;
-- src:747 | (b) a registrar, transfer agent or branch transfer agent of the corporation, or an individual on their behalf; and
-- src:748 | (c) a trustee who certifies it in accordance with a trust indenture.
@ref CBCA s 49(4) (src:744-748)
GIVEN `the signature of a director or officer of the corporation is on the certificate, signed or printed or mechanically reproduced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the signature of a registrar, transfer agent or branch transfer agent of the corporation or of an individual on their behalf is on the certificate, signed or printed or mechanically reproduced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the signature of a trustee who certifies the certificate in accordance with a trust indenture is on the certificate, signed or printed or mechanically reproduced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a security certificate is signed as required within s 49(4)` MEANS
        `the signature of a director or officer of the corporation is on the certificate, signed or printed or mechanically reproduced`
    OR  `the signature of a registrar, transfer agent or branch transfer agent of the corporation or of an individual on their behalf is on the certificate, signed or printed or mechanically reproduced`
    OR  `the signature of a trustee who certifies the certificate in accordance with a trust indenture is on the certificate, signed or printed or mechanically reproduced`

§§ `s 49(5) [Repealed]`

-- Repealed in this text: see the coverage table.

§§ `s 49(6) Continuation of signature`

-- src:750 | Continuation of signature
-- src:751 | (6) If a security certificate contains a printed or mechanically reproduced signature of a person, the corporation may issue the security certificate, notwithstanding that the person has ceased to be a director or an officer of the corporation, and the security certificate is as valid as if the person were a director or an officer at the date of its issue.
@ref CBCA s 49(6) (src:750-751)
GIVEN `the certificate contains a printed or mechanically reproduced signature of a person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may issue the certificate within s 49(6)` MEANS
    `the certificate contains a printed or mechanically reproduced signature of a person`

-- The certificate "is as valid as if the person were a director or an officer at the date of its issue":
-- the person is treated as a director or officer for the signature, whether or not they still are.
-- src:750 | Continuation of signature
-- src:751 | (6) If a security certificate contains a printed or mechanically reproduced signature of a person, the corporation may issue the security certificate, notwithstanding that the person has ceased to be a director or an officer of the corporation, and the security certificate is as valid as if the person were a director or an officer at the date of its issue.
@ref CBCA s 49(6) (src:750-751)
GIVEN `the certificate contains a printed or mechanically reproduced signature of a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has ceased to be a director or an officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the signature is treated as that of a director or officer at the date of issue within s 49(6)` MEANS
        `the certificate contains a printed or mechanically reproduced signature of a person`
    AND `the person has ceased to be a director or an officer of the corporation`

§§ `s 49(7) Contents of share certificate`

-- The face of each share certificate states (a) the name of the corporation, (b) one of two forms of
-- words, (c) the name of the person to whom it was issued, (d) the number and class of shares and the
-- designation of any series.
-- src:752 | Contents of share certificate
-- src:753 | (7) There shall be stated on the face of each share certificate issued by a corporation
-- src:754 | (a) the name of the corporation;
-- src:755 | (b) the words “Incorporated under the Canada Business Corporations Act” or “subject to the Canada Business Corporations Act”;
-- src:756 | (c) the name of the person to whom it was issued; and
-- src:757 | (d) the number and class of shares and the designation of any series that the certificate represents.
@ref CBCA s 49(7) (src:752-757)
GIVEN `the face states the name of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the face states the words "Incorporated under the Canada Business Corporations Act" or "subject to the Canada Business Corporations Act"` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the face states the name of the person to whom the certificate was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the face states the number and class of shares and the designation of any series that the certificate represents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a share certificate states what it must on its face within s 49(7)` MEANS
        `the face states the name of the corporation`
    AND `the face states the words "Incorporated under the Canada Business Corporations Act" or "subject to the Canada Business Corporations Act"`
    AND `the face states the name of the person to whom the certificate was issued`
    AND `the face states the number and class of shares and the designation of any series that the certificate represents`

§§ `s 49(8) Restrictions`

-- Four kinds of item are named; a constraint under s 174 is carved out of (a) (out of range: section 174 (piece cb4);
-- out of range: section 190(10) (piece cb4)). The answer constructors say which kind the item is.
-- src:758 | Restrictions
-- src:759 | (8) No restriction, charge, lien, hypothec, agreement or endorsement described in the following paragraphs is effective against a transferee of a security, issued by a corporation or by a body corporate before the body corporate was continued under this Act, who has no actual knowledge of the restriction, charge, lien, hypothec, agreement or endorsement unless it or a reference to it is noted conspicuously on the security certificate:
-- src:760 | (a) a restriction on transfer other than a constraint under section 174;
-- src:761 | (b) a charge, lien or hypothec in favour of the corporation;
-- src:762 | (c) a unanimous shareholder agreement; or
-- src:763 | (d) an endorsement under subsection 190(10).
@ref CBCA s 49(8) (src:758-763)
DECLARE `Kind of item that must be noted on a certificate under s 49(8)` IS ONE OF
    `a restriction on transfer other than a constraint under section 174`
    `a charge, lien or hypothec in favour of the corporation`
    `a unanimous shareholder agreement as an item under s 49(8)`
    `an endorsement under subsection 190(10)`
    `a constraint under section 174 as an item under s 49(8)`
    `an item of none of these kinds under s 49(8)`

-- TRUE when s 49(8) makes the item ineffective against the transferee: the security was issued by a
-- corporation (or by a body corporate before it was continued under this Act), the item is one of the
-- four kinds, the transferee has no actual knowledge of it, and neither it nor a reference to it is noted
-- conspicuously on the certificate. FALSE means only that s 49(8) does not make it ineffective (the
-- transferee knew, it was noted, or it is not one of the four kinds); whether it is then effective is
-- for other law.
-- src:758 | Restrictions
-- src:759 | (8) No restriction, charge, lien, hypothec, agreement or endorsement described in the following paragraphs is effective against a transferee of a security, issued by a corporation or by a body corporate before the body corporate was continued under this Act, who has no actual knowledge of the restriction, charge, lien, hypothec, agreement or endorsement unless it or a reference to it is noted conspicuously on the security certificate:
-- src:760 | (a) a restriction on transfer other than a constraint under section 174;
-- src:761 | (b) a charge, lien or hypothec in favour of the corporation;
-- src:762 | (c) a unanimous shareholder agreement; or
-- src:763 | (d) an endorsement under subsection 190(10).
@ref CBCA s 49(8) (src:758-763)
GIVEN `the security was issued by a corporation or by a body corporate before it was continued under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of item` IS A `Kind of item that must be noted on a certificate under s 49(8)`
      `the transferee has actual knowledge of the item` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the item or a reference to it is noted conspicuously on the security certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the item is ineffective against the transferee within s 49(8)` MEANS
        `the security was issued by a corporation or by a body corporate before it was continued under this Act`
    AND (   `the kind of item` EQUALS `a restriction on transfer other than a constraint under section 174`
         OR `the kind of item` EQUALS `a charge, lien or hypothec in favour of the corporation`
         OR `the kind of item` EQUALS `a unanimous shareholder agreement as an item under s 49(8)`
         OR `the kind of item` EQUALS `an endorsement under subsection 190(10)`)
    AND (NOT `the transferee has actual knowledge of the item`)
    AND (NOT `the item or a reference to it is noted conspicuously on the security certificate`)

§§ `s 49(9) Limit on restriction`

-- A distributing corporation, any of whose issued shares remain outstanding and are held by more than one
-- person, shall not have a restriction on the transfer or ownership of its shares except a constraint
-- permitted under s 174. JUST TRUE: permitted; JUST FALSE: forbidden; NOTHING: s 49(9) does not apply.
-- out of range: section 174 (piece cb4)
-- src:764 | Limit on restriction
-- src:765 | (9) A distributing corporation, any of the issued shares of which remain outstanding and are held by more than one person, shall not have a restriction on the transfer or ownership of its shares of any class or series except by way of a constraint permitted under section 174.
@ref CBCA s 49(9) (src:764-765)
GIVEN `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `issued shares of the corporation remain outstanding and are held by more than one person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the restriction is a constraint permitted under section 174` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the corporation may have the restriction on transfer or ownership within s 49(9)` MEANS
    IF     `the corporation is a distributing corporation`
       AND `issued shares of the corporation remain outstanding and are held by more than one person`
    THEN JUST `the restriction is a constraint permitted under section 174`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 49(10) Notation of constraint`

-- Where the articles constrain the issue, transfer or ownership of shares for purpose (a) (Canadian
-- ownership or control under a prescribed law) or (b) (compliance with a prescribed law), the constraint or
-- a reference to it must be noted conspicuously on every certificate for a constrained share issued AFTER
-- the day the share became subject to the constraint under this Act.
-- src:766 | Notation of constraint
-- src:767 | (10) Where the articles of a corporation constrain the issue, transfer or ownership of shares of any class or series in order to assist
-- src:768 | (a) the corporation or any of its affiliates or associates to qualify under any prescribed law of Canada or a province to receive licences, permits, grants, payments or other benefits by reason of attaining or maintaining a specified level of Canadian ownership or control, or
-- src:769 | (b) the corporation to comply with any prescribed law,
-- src:770 | the constraint, or a reference to it, shall be conspicuously noted on every security certificate of the corporation evidencing a share that is subject to the constraint where the security certificate is issued after the day on which the share becomes subject to the constraint under this Act.
@ref CBCA s 49(10) (src:766-770)
GIVEN `the articles constrain the issue, transfer or ownership of shares to assist the corporation or an affiliate or associate to qualify under a law prescribed by the regulations for benefits by reason of a specified level of Canadian ownership or control` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles constrain the issue, transfer or ownership of shares to assist the corporation to comply with a law prescribed by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate evidences a share that is subject to the constraint` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the certificate is issued` IS A DATE
      `the day the share becomes subject to the constraint under this Act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the constraint must be noted conspicuously on the certificate within s 49(10)` MEANS
        (   `the articles constrain the issue, transfer or ownership of shares to assist the corporation or an affiliate or associate to qualify under a law prescribed by the regulations for benefits by reason of a specified level of Canadian ownership or control`
         OR `the articles constrain the issue, transfer or ownership of shares to assist the corporation to comply with a law prescribed by the regulations`)
    AND `the certificate evidences a share that is subject to the constraint`
    AND `the day the certificate is issued` GREATER THAN `the day the share becomes subject to the constraint under this Act`

§§ `s 49(11) Failure to note`

-- NOTHING: there was no failure to note a constraint under (10), so s 49(11) says nothing.
-- src:771 | Failure to note
-- src:772 | (11) The failure to note a constraint or a reference to it pursuant to subsection (10) shall not invalidate any share or security certificate and shall not render a constraint ineffective against an owner, holder or transferee of the share or security certificate.
@ref CBCA s 49(11) (src:771-772)
GIVEN `there was a failure to note a constraint or a reference to it pursuant to subsection 49(10)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the failure to note invalidates a share or certificate or makes the constraint ineffective within s 49(11)` MEANS
    IF `there was a failure to note a constraint or a reference to it pursuant to subsection 49(10)`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 49(12) Transitional`

-- src:773 | Transitional
-- src:774 | (12) If a body corporate continued under this Act has outstanding security certificates, and if the words “private company” appear on the certificates, those words are deemed to be a notice of a restriction, lien, hypothec, agreement or endorsement for the purpose of subsection (8).
@ref CBCA s 49(12) (src:773-774)
GIVEN `the body corporate was continued under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has outstanding security certificates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the words "private company" appear on the certificates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the words "private company" are deemed notice of a restriction, lien, hypothec, agreement or endorsement within s 49(12)` MEANS
        `the body corporate was continued under this Act`
    AND `it has outstanding security certificates`
    AND `the words "private company" appear on the certificates`

§§ `s 49(13) Particulars of class`

-- A share certificate of a corporation authorized to issue more than one class or series states legibly
-- (a) the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions of each class and series existing when it is
-- issued, or (b) that they exist and that the corporation will furnish a full copy on demand and without
-- charge. TRUE when met, and TRUE when the corporation has only one class and series.
-- src:775 | Particulars of class
-- src:776 | (13) There shall be stated legibly on a share certificate issued by a corporation that is authorized to issue shares of more than one class or series
-- src:777 | (a) the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attached to the shares of each class and series that exists when the share certificate is issued; or
-- src:778 | (b) that the class or series of shares that it represents has rights, privileges, restrictions or conditions attached thereto and that the corporation will furnish a shareholder, on demand and without charge, with a full copy of the text of
-- src:779 | (i) the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attached to each class authorized to be issued and to each series in so far as the same have been fixed by the directors, and
-- src:780 | (ii) the authority of the directors to fix the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions of subsequent series.
@ref CBCA s 49(13) (src:775-780)
GIVEN `the corporation is authorized to issue shares of more than one class or series` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states legibly the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attached to the shares of each class and series that exists when it is issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states legibly that the class or series has rights, privileges, restrictions or conditions attached and that the corporation will furnish a full copy of their text on demand and without charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a share certificate gives the particulars of the class or series within s 49(13)` MEANS
        (NOT `the corporation is authorized to issue shares of more than one class or series`)
    OR  `the certificate states legibly the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attached to the shares of each class and series that exists when it is issued`
    OR  `the certificate states legibly that the class or series has rights, privileges, restrictions or conditions attached and that the corporation will furnish a full copy of their text on demand and without charge`

§§ `s 49(14) Duty`

-- src:781 | Duty
-- src:782 | (14) Where a share certificate issued by a corporation contains the statement mentioned in paragraph (13)(b), the corporation shall furnish a shareholder, on demand and without charge, with a full copy of the text of
-- src:783 | (a) the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attached to each class authorized to be issued and to each series in so far as the same have been fixed by the directors; and
-- src:784 | (b) the authority of the directors to fix the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions of subsequent series.
@ref CBCA s 49(14) (src:781-784)
GIVEN `the share certificate contains the statement mentioned in paragraph 49(13)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person asking is a shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shareholder demands a full copy of the text` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must furnish a full copy of the text on demand within s 49(14)` MEANS
        `the share certificate contains the statement mentioned in paragraph 49(13)(b)`
    AND `the person asking is a shareholder`
    AND `the shareholder demands a full copy of the text`

-- "without charge": the most the corporation may charge for the copy is nothing. NOTHING: the duty does
-- not arise, so s 49(14) says nothing about a charge.
-- src:781 | Duty
-- src:782 | (14) Where a share certificate issued by a corporation contains the statement mentioned in paragraph (13)(b), the corporation shall furnish a shareholder, on demand and without charge, with a full copy of the text of
-- src:783 | (a) the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions attached to each class authorized to be issued and to each series in so far as the same have been fixed by the directors; and
-- src:784 | (b) the authority of the directors to fix the rights, privileges, restrictions and conditions of subsequent series.
@ref CBCA s 49(14) (src:781-784)
GIVEN `the share certificate contains the statement mentioned in paragraph 49(13)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person asking is a shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shareholder demands a full copy of the text` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the most the corporation may charge for the copy in dollars within s 49(14)` MEANS
    IF     `the share certificate contains the statement mentioned in paragraph 49(13)(b)`
       AND `the person asking is a shareholder`
       AND `the shareholder demands a full copy of the text`
    THEN JUST 0
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 49(15) Fractional share`

-- src:785 | Fractional share
-- src:786 | (15) A corporation may issue for each fractional share, a certificate in registered form or scrip certificates in registered form that entitle the holder to receive a certificate for a full share in exchange for scrip certificates equalling a full share.
@ref CBCA s 49(15) (src:785-786)
GIVEN `the share is a fractional share` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate or each scrip certificate is in registered form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may issue a certificate or scrip certificates for the fractional share within s 49(15)` MEANS
        `the share is a fractional share`
    AND `the certificate or each scrip certificate is in registered form`

-- Scrip certificates "equalling a full share" entitle the holder to a certificate for a full share in
-- exchange. The fractions the holder's scrip certificates represent are added; each whole share's worth
-- may be exchanged (fork F-P7-3 in NOTES.md: a remainder under a whole share is not exchangeable).
-- src:785 | Fractional share
-- src:786 | (15) A corporation may issue for each fractional share, a certificate in registered form or scrip certificates in registered form that entitle the holder to receive a certificate for a full share in exchange for scrip certificates equalling a full share.
@ref CBCA s 49(15) (src:785-786)
GIVEN `the fractions of a share that the holder's scrip certificates represent, added together` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of full-share certificates the holder may receive in exchange within s 49(15)` MEANS
    FLOOR `the fractions of a share that the holder's scrip certificates represent, added together`

§§ `s 49(15.1) Replacement`

-- "before the coming into force of this subsection": the text does not give the date, so the day
-- subsection 49(15.1) came into force is a plain input.
-- src:787 | Replacement
-- src:788 | (15.1) On the request of a holder of a certificate for a fractional share or of a scrip certificate, a corporation shall, if the certificate is in bearer form and was issued before the coming into force of this subsection, issue in exchange to that holder, in registered form, a certificate for a fractional share or a scrip certificate, as the case may be.
@ref CBCA s 49(15.1) (src:787-788)
GIVEN `the holder requests an exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate is for a fractional share or is a scrip certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate is in bearer form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the certificate was issued` IS A DATE
      `the day subsection 49(15.1) came into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must issue a registered-form certificate in exchange within s 49(15.1)` MEANS
        `the holder requests an exchange`
    AND `the certificate is for a fractional share or is a scrip certificate`
    AND `the certificate is in bearer form`
    AND `the day the certificate was issued` LESS THAN `the day subsection 49(15.1) came into force`

§§ `s 49(16) Scrip certificates`

-- (a) The directors may make a scrip certificate void (or null, in Quebec) if it is not exchanged for a
-- share certificate representing a full share before a specified date. Read as: once the specified date
-- is reached with no exchange having been made before it, the scrip certificate is void.
-- src:789 | Scrip certificates
-- src:790 | (16) The directors may attach conditions to any scrip certificates issued by a corporation, including conditions that
-- src:791 | (a) the scrip certificates become void or, in Quebec, null if not exchanged for a share certificate representing a full share before a specified date; and
-- src:792 | (b) any shares for which such scrip certificates are exchangeable may, notwithstanding any pre-emptive right, be issued by the corporation to any person and the proceeds thereof distributed rateably to the holders of the scrip certificates.
@ref CBCA s 49(16)(a) (src:789-792)
GIVEN `the directors attached a condition that unexchanged scrip certificates become void` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the scrip certificate was exchanged for a share certificate representing a full share before the specified date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the specified date` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the scrip certificate has become void within s 49(16)(a)` MEANS
        `the directors attached a condition that unexchanged scrip certificates become void`
    AND (NOT `the scrip certificate was exchanged for a share certificate representing a full share before the specified date`)
    AND `the day asked about` AT LEAST `the specified date`

-- (b) The directors may provide that shares for which scrip certificates are exchangeable may, despite any
-- pre-emptive right, be issued to any person, and the proceeds distributed rateably to the holders.
-- src:789 | Scrip certificates
-- src:790 | (16) The directors may attach conditions to any scrip certificates issued by a corporation, including conditions that
-- src:791 | (a) the scrip certificates become void or, in Quebec, null if not exchanged for a share certificate representing a full share before a specified date; and
-- src:792 | (b) any shares for which such scrip certificates are exchangeable may, notwithstanding any pre-emptive right, be issued by the corporation to any person and the proceeds thereof distributed rateably to the holders of the scrip certificates.
@ref CBCA s 49(16)(b) (src:789-792)
GIVEN `the directors attached a condition that the shares may be issued to any person and the proceeds distributed rateably to the holders of the scrip certificates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the shares may be issued to any person despite a pre-emptive right within s 49(16)(b)` MEANS
    `the directors attached a condition that the shares may be issued to any person and the proceeds distributed rateably to the holders of the scrip certificates`

-- Rateably: each holder's share of the proceeds is in proportion to the scrip they hold. NOTHING: no scrip
-- is outstanding, so there is nothing to divide by.
-- src:789 | Scrip certificates
-- src:790 | (16) The directors may attach conditions to any scrip certificates issued by a corporation, including conditions that
-- src:791 | (a) the scrip certificates become void or, in Quebec, null if not exchanged for a share certificate representing a full share before a specified date; and
-- src:792 | (b) any shares for which such scrip certificates are exchangeable may, notwithstanding any pre-emptive right, be issued by the corporation to any person and the proceeds thereof distributed rateably to the holders of the scrip certificates.
@ref CBCA s 49(16)(b) (src:789-792)
GIVEN `the proceeds in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the scrip certificates the holder holds, as fractions of a share, added together` IS A NUMBER
      `all the scrip certificates outstanding, as fractions of a share, added together` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the holder's rateable share of the proceeds in dollars within s 49(16)(b)` MEANS
    IF `all the scrip certificates outstanding, as fractions of a share, added together` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST (`the proceeds in dollars`
               TIMES (`the scrip certificates the holder holds, as fractions of a share, added together`
                      DIVIDED BY `all the scrip certificates outstanding, as fractions of a share, added together`))
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 49(17) Holder of fractional share`

-- Not entitled to exercise voting rights or to receive a dividend in respect of the fractional share,
-- unless (a) it results from a consolidation of shares or (b) the articles otherwise provide. TRUE when the
-- bar applies; FALSE means only that s 49(17) does not bar the holder.
-- src:793 | Holder of fractional share
-- src:794 | (17) A holder of a fractional share issued by a corporation is not entitled to exercise voting rights or to receive a dividend in respect of the fractional share, unless
-- src:795 | (a) the fractional share results from a consolidation of shares; or
-- src:796 | (b) the articles of the corporation otherwise provide.
@ref CBCA s 49(17) (src:793-796)
GIVEN `the person holds a fractional share` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fractional share results from a consolidation of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles of the corporation otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the holder of the fractional share is barred from voting and from dividends within s 49(17)` MEANS
        `the person holds a fractional share`
    AND (NOT `the fractional share results from a consolidation of shares`)
    AND (NOT `the articles of the corporation otherwise provide`)

§§ `s 49(18) Holder of scrip certificate`

-- src:797 | Holder of scrip certificate
-- src:798 | (18) A holder of a scrip certificate is not entitled to exercise voting rights or to receive a dividend in respect of the scrip certificate.
@ref CBCA s 49(18) (src:797-798)
GIVEN `the person holds a scrip certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the holder of the scrip certificate is barred from voting and from dividends within s 49(18)` MEANS
    `the person holds a scrip certificate`
